{'kind':'p','text':"Plan 14-24 months from first design meeting to move-in: 3-6 months of design and engineering, 1-4 months of permitting and HOA review, then 12-18 months of construction. Construction costs $400-$725+ per heated square foot in 2026. Schedules slip most often on selections and permitting, not framing."},
{'kind':'p','text':"UPDATED APRIL 2026",'cap':true},
{'kind':'p','text':"The design-build approach eliminates the traditional gap between architect and builder — creating a single-source partnership where design vision and construction expertise inform each other from the very first conversation. Peters Custom Homes offers Charlotte families an integrated design-build experience where architecture, interior design, and construction are coordinated under one professional team."},
{'kind':'p','text':"This integrated approach prevents the cost overruns, design conflicts, and communication breakdowns that frequently plague traditional architect-bid-build projects. When designer and builder share the same goals, families benefit from homes that are both architecturally ambitious and practically buildable within budget."},
{'kind':'h2','text':"Our Approach"},
{'kind':'p','text':"Peters Custom Homes coordinates experienced architects and interior designers as part of our comprehensive design-build service. This integration ensures that design decisions are informed by real construction costs, material availability, and structural feasibility — eliminating the \"design it, then figure out how to build it\" approach that inflates costs."},
{'kind':'p','text':"Our design-build process typically saves families 15-20% compared to traditional architect-bid-build, while delivering homes that are equally (or more) architecturally distinguished."},
{'kind':'h2','text':"Architectural Collaboration"},
{'kind':'p','text':"Collaboration is the cornerstone of design-build excellence. Our process brings architect, interior designer, structural engineer, and builder to the same table from day one — ensuring every design decision is informed by construction reality and every construction decision respects design intent."},
{'kind':'h2','text':"Process & Stewardship"},
{'kind':'p','text':"Design-build construction eliminates the adversarial dynamics that sometimes develop between architects and builders in traditional delivery. Our team shares a single goal: delivering your dream home on time, on budget, and at the highest quality standard."},
{'kind':'h2','text':"Living in Charlotte"},
{'kind':'p','text':"Charlotte families increasingly prefer design-build for luxury custom homes because it offers a single point of accountability, streamlined communication, and the confidence that their builder understands their architect's intent — because they've been working together from the beginning."},
{'kind':'h2','text':"Frequently Asked Questions"},
{'kind':'h3','text':"What is in-house design-build?"},
{'kind':'p','text':"In-house design-build means architecture and construction operate under one roof, providing single-point accountability, integrated cost planning, faster timelines, and seamless communication. Peters Custom Homes, Inc. coordinates with Emerald & Oak Design , a separate interior design business the homeowner engages under its own agreement."},
{'kind':'h3','text':"How do I begin the process of building with Peters Custom Homes?"},
{'kind':'p','text':"Every engagement begins with a private consultation where we learn about your family's vision, timeline, and goals. From there, we guide you through homesite evaluation, architect selection, design development, and the full scope of pre-construction planning. We accept a limited number of new engagements each year, so we encourage interested families to reach out early to discuss availability."},
{'kind':'h3','text':"What sets a Peters Custom Home apart after move-in?"},
{'kind':'p','text':"The difference reveals itself in the details you experience daily—doors that close with a whisper, natural light that shifts beautifully through carefully placed windows, materials that age gracefully, and mechanical systems that perform silently and efficiently. Our families consistently tell us that the quality of daily life in their home exceeds even their highest expectations, and that the residence continues to surprise and delight years after completion."},
{'kind':'h3','text':"CONTINUE EXPLORING"}
